      "content": "that makes sense. but if you say it's possible to capture the tone and the phrasing, then wouldn't that be \"close enough\" to fool people in a text or chat? like if someone can't see your face or hear your voice, how would they even know it isn't you? what kind of specific patterns or \"tells\" should i be looking for to see if the person i'm talking to is actually my friend or just a version of me being used to mirror them?",
